{"data": [{"author_id": "778764142412984320", "created_at": "2026-11-05T19:50:50.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118430862949945612"], "id": "2118430862949945612", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 25, "impression_count": 6393, "like_count": 46, "quote_count": 4, "reply_count": 21, "retweet_count": 7}, "text": "Our open-source ML Intern is now available as a Slack bot you can install in your own workspace! \n\nEvaluate models, build datasets, and fine-tune models on the fly 🚀 https://t.co/KrlSi3K6sY", "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "x.com/abidlabs/statu…", "end": 189, "expanded_url": "https://twitter.com/abidlabs/status/2118429900134871418", "start": 166, "url": "https://t.co/KrlSi3K6sY"}]}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2118429900134871418", "type": "quoted"}], "url": "https://x.com/huggingface/status/2118430862949945612"}, {"author_id": "2939913921", "created_at": "2026-11-05T19:29:24.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118425465988014534"], "id": "2118425465988014534", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 11, "impression_count": 3607, "like_count": 52, "quote_count": 1, "reply_count": 14, "retweet_count": 2}, "text": "imo a lack of good enough benchmarks is a bottleneck. At least for the type of RSI describe as an intelligence explosion. You can use existing benchmarks to make models way cheaper, though. https://t.co/pKNJmUCDv4 https://t.co/iOffCwbh5D", "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/pKNJmUCDv4", "end": 213, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/natolambert/status/2118425465988014534/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2118425293857697792", "start": 190, "url": "https://t.co/pKNJmUCDv4"}, {"display_url": "x.com/METR_Evals/sta…", "end": 237, "expanded_url": "https://twitter.com/METR_Evals/status/2118412183860351084", "start": 214, "url": "https://t.co/iOffCwbh5D"}]}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2118412183860351084", "type": "quoted"}], "url": "https://x.com/natolambert/status/2118425465988014534"}, {"author_id": "1745106082790318080", "created_at": "2026-11-05T19:07:09.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118419869091713083"], "id": "2118419869091713083", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 31, "impression_count": 14701, "like_count": 82, "quote_count": 2, "reply_count": 15, "retweet_count": 9}, "text": "The Iron(wood) Throne: \nGoogle's TPU Stakes Its Claim on Inference\nViable Alternative of CUDA Moat, \nNVIDIA Working Nights &amp; Weekends, \nJensen’s Counter Submission, Kimi K3, \nMeta Muse Spark Open, GLM5.3, \nTorchTPU, SGLang, vLLM, llm-d, Ray \nhttps://t.co/mh16HIWmpJ", "entities": {"urls": [{"description": "Viable Alternative of CUDA Moat, NVIDIA scared and working nights & weekends, Jensen’s Counter Submission, Kimi K3, Muse Spark Open, Qwen, GLM5.3, TorchTPU, vLLM, SGLang, llm-d, Ray", "display_url": "newsletter.semianalysis.com/p/tpu-strikes-…", "end": 269, "expanded_url": "https://newsletter.semianalysis.com/p/tpu-strikes-the-king", "images": [{"height": 800, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2118419871969026049/AGuO_fYS?format=jpg&name=orig", "width": 1600}, {"height": 150, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2118419871969026049/AGuO_fYS?format=jpg&name=150x150", "width": 150}], "start": 246, "status": 200, "title": "The Iron(wood) Throne: Google's TPU Stakes Its Claim on Inference", "unwound_url": "https://newsletter.semianalysis.com/p/tpu-strikes-the-king", "url": "https://t.co/mh16HIWmpJ"}]}, "url": "https://x.com/SemiAnalysis_/status/2118419869091713083"}, {"author_id": "1034844617261248512", "created_at": "2026-11-05T18:36:25.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118412135340572850"], "id": "2118412135340572850", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 34, "impression_count": 19287, "like_count": 189, "quote_count": 22, "reply_count": 39, "retweet_count": 19}, "text": "During Connect, we previewed Muse Realtime Avatar, our real-time embodiment technology that turns Muse Realtime Voice into expressive, interactive avatars.\n\nToday, we’re rolling it out in the @Muse app in the US, giving people a more natural way to engage with their personal https://t.co/QYU6Pg8Fch", "entities": {"mentions": [{"end": 197, "id": "2052434492263178240", "start": 192, "username": "Muse"}], "urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/QYU6Pg8Fch", "end": 299, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/AIatMeta/status/2118412135340572850/video/1", "media_key": "13_2118411815852056576", "start": 276, "url": "https://t.co/QYU6Pg8Fch"}]}, "url": "https://x.com/AIatMeta/status/2118412135340572850"}, {"author_id": "1745106082790318080", "created_at": "2026-11-05T18:36:07.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118412057204654176"], "id": "2118412057204654176", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 15, "impression_count": 15426, "like_count": 67, "quote_count": 3, "reply_count": 14, "retweet_count": 2}, "text": "Advantest and Teradyne both reported 3Q26 this week. We believe the two calls say the same thing: the ATE TAM is growing on AI compute, and supply, not demand, is the constraint through 2027. (1/5)🧵 https://t.co/phQBfzLEAB", "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/phQBfzLEAB", "end": 222, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/SemiAnalysis_/status/2118412057204654176/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2118412054075678720", "start": 199, "url": "https://t.co/phQBfzLEAB"}]}, "url": "https://x.com/SemiAnalysis_/status/2118412057204654176"}, {"author_id": "2465283662", "created_at": "2026-11-05T17:51:51.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118400919637508576"], "id": "2118400919637508576", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 20, "impression_count": 5076, "like_count": 38, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 9, "retweet_count": 5}, "text": "From Pixels to Actions \n\nTowards Native Vision-Language-Action Policies\n\npaper: https://t.co/8eyxEVpjnI https://t.co/JodXyKkSZ9", "entities": {"urls": [{"description": "Join the discussion on this paper page", "display_url": "huggingface.co/papers/2611.06…", "end": 103, "expanded_url": "https://huggingface.co/papers/2611.06918", "images": [{"height": 648, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2118400922925895682/9QNsS_N2?format=jpg&name=orig", "width": 1200}, {"height": 150, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2118400922925895682/9QNsS_N2?format=jpg&name=150x150", "width": 150}], "start": 80, "status": 200, "title": "Paper page - From Pixels to Actions - Towards Native Vision-Language-Action Policies", "unwound_url": "https://huggingface.co/papers/2611.06918", "url": "https://t.co/8eyxEVpjnI"}, {"display_url": "pic.x.com/JodXyKkSZ9", "end": 127, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/_akhaliq/status/2118400919637508576/video/1", "media_key": "13_2118400803350417408", "start": 104, "url": "https://t.co/JodXyKkSZ9"}]}, "url": "https://x.com/_akhaliq/status/2118400919637508576"}, {"author_id": "4398626122", "created_at": "2026-11-05T17:09:13.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118390190246879554"], "id": "2118390190246879554", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 1568, "impression_count": 964550, "like_count": 10656, "quote_count": 650, "reply_count": 726, "retweet_count": 903}, "text": "Introducing GPT‑6 Cyber: a major advance in security research that pairs stronger capabilities with better model alignment.\n\nThe model powered the Linux kernel research we announced yesterday, and security teams at companies like Mozilla, Palo Alto Networks, Calif, and https://t.co/34uAeNnhwP", "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/34uAeNnhwP", "end": 293, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/OpenAI/status/2118390190246879554/video/1", "media_key": "13_2118387217588465664", "start": 270, "url": "https://t.co/34uAeNnhwP"}]}, "url": "https://x.com/OpenAI/status/2118390190246879554"}, {"author_id": "1529761561170124800", "created_at": "2026-11-05T17:08:38.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118390043249434915"], "id": "2118390043249434915", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 24, "impression_count": 5336, "like_count": 105, "quote_count": 3, "reply_count": 9, "retweet_count": 15}, "text": "About 1 in 4 US workers (26%) used a paid AI service for their job in the past week, according to our October poll. This includes AI paid for by their employer, by themselves, or by both.\n\nAnother 15% used only free versions, and 55% didn’t use AI for work at all in the past https://t.co/wHohobwhQG", "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/wHohobwhQG", "end": 299, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/EpochAIResearch/status/2118390043249434915/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2118390040401432576", "start": 276, "url": "https://t.co/wHohobwhQG"}]}, "url": "https://x.com/EpochAIResearch/status/2118390043249434915"}, {"author_id": "1529761561170124800", "created_at": "2026-11-05T17:01:01.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118388127337517276"], "id": "2118388127337517276", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 14, "impression_count": 4112, "like_count": 89, "quote_count": 1, "reply_count": 9, "retweet_count": 9}, "text": "Broadcom TPU compute shipments doubled from fiscal Q2 to Q3 2026 (May to early August), reaching the equivalent of nearly 2 million Nvidia H100 GPUs, according to our estimates.\n\nThis is a sharp increase from the previous three quarters, when shipments grew 2–22% per quarter. https://t.co/sYIysfzhxh", "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/sYIysfzhxh", "end": 300, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/EpochAIResearch/status/2118388127337517276/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2118388124267208705", "start": 277, "url": "https://t.co/sYIysfzhxh"}]}, "url": "https://x.com/EpochAIResearch/status/2118388127337517276"}, {"author_id": "1745106082790318080", "created_at": "2026-11-05T15:34:59.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118366474112790630"], "id": "2118366474112790630", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 18, "impression_count": 22231, "like_count": 133, "quote_count": 2, "reply_count": 17, "retweet_count": 7}, "text": "Congrats to the Nvidia team working on VR! As Muse spark open throughput runs faster on VR hardware, the software is also developing at breakneck speeds 🏃💨 enabling faster support for newer models. This is part of the CUDA moat 🟩, fast hardware and fast development! (1/2)🧵 https://t.co/EMTBeCqLCj", "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/EMTBeCqLCj", "end": 297, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/SemiAnalysis_/status/2118366474112790630/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2118366471420047360", "start": 274, "url": "https://t.co/EMTBeCqLCj"}]}, "url": "https://x.com/SemiAnalysis_/status/2118366474112790630"}, {"author_id": "2939913921", "created_at": "2026-11-05T15:21:07.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118362983285850288"], "id": "2118362983285850288", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 723, "impression_count": 36818, "like_count": 1150, "quote_count": 3, "reply_count": 41, "retweet_count": 32}, "text": "I regularly hear from people that my post-training book/writing has helped them get a job at labs by focusing on material that develops intuitions for how training methods work. It's very validating, because this type of \"idea/math heavy\" writing doesn't really sell many books.", "url": "https://x.com/natolambert/status/2118362983285850288"}, {"author_id": "2939913921", "created_at": "2026-11-05T15:07:29.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118359553532481655"], "id": "2118359553532481655", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 213, "impression_count": 12337, "like_count": 270, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 14, "retweet_count": 13}, "text": "Have heard from many folks that score-centering is popular in industry (e.g. Tinker's StableReinforce using it), so it's the latest addition to the rlhf book. It's a nice derivation to understand training-inference-mismatch.\n\nVideo version explaining it soon. https://t.co/b3SJaElgSo", "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "x.com/mrtnm/status/2…", "end": 283, "expanded_url": "https://twitter.com/mrtnm/status/2100997113903477121", "start": 260, "url": "https://t.co/b3SJaElgSo"}]}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2100997113903477121", "type": "quoted"}], "url": "https://x.com/natolambert/status/2118359553532481655"}, {"author_id": "778764142412984320", "created_at": "2026-11-05T11:36:58.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118306577203822976"], "id": "2118306577203822976", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 269, "impression_count": 32622, "like_count": 475, "quote_count": 14, "reply_count": 75, "retweet_count": 79}, "text": "Join us in this livestream next Tuesday, learn how to shrink models to fit in your laptop and make them go brrr 💨\n\nWe will have @mervenoyann @maximelabonne @TadimetiAditya @bartowski1182  and @mgoin_ giving a primer and know-hows on quantization with llama.cpp and vLLM ⚡️ https://t.co/JXjQUouVM4", "entities": {"mentions": [{"end": 140, "id": "1202267633049100291", "start": 128, "username": "mervenoyann"}, {"end": 155, "id": "923114064460558336", "start": 141, "username": "maximelabonne"}, {"end": 171, "id": "1042984647125168128", "start": 156, "username": "TadimetiAditya"}, {"end": 186, "id": "1756145750759620608", "start": 172, "username": "bartowski1182"}, {"end": 199, "id": "1516059175910092803", "start": 192, "username": "mgoin_"}], "urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/JXjQUouVM4", "end": 296, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/huggingface/status/2118306577203822976/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2118305709930467328", "start": 273, "url": "https://t.co/JXjQUouVM4"}]}, "url": "https://x.com/huggingface/status/2118306577203822976"}, {"author_id": "1745106082790318080", "created_at": "2026-11-05T05:00:15.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118206738255983083"], "id": "2118206738255983083", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 12, "impression_count": 25579, "like_count": 99, "quote_count": 3, "reply_count": 12, "retweet_count": 4}, "text": "A silicon face to face: Huawei's Kirin 9050 Pro hybrid-bonded logic die, direct from SemiAnalysis’ Teardown Lab. https://t.co/7lfK8R6Vqt", "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/7lfK8R6Vqt", "end": 136, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/SemiAnalysis_/status/2118206738255983083/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2118206735978553344", "start": 113, "url": "https://t.co/7lfK8R6Vqt"}]}, "url": "https://x.com/SemiAnalysis_/status/2118206738255983083"}, {"author_id": "2939913921", "created_at": "2026-11-05T00:26:33.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118137858112499779"], "id": "2118137858112499779", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 57, "impression_count": 23714, "like_count": 384, "quote_count": 2, "reply_count": 32, "retweet_count": 14}, "text": "Post-training and post-post-training are really different arts", "url": "https://x.com/natolambert/status/2118137858112499779"}, {"author_id": "1745106082790318080", "created_at": "2026-11-05T00:09:33.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118133582979813819"], "id": "2118133582979813819", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 223, "impression_count": 307831, "like_count": 775, "quote_count": 72, "reply_count": 194, "retweet_count": 44}, "text": "BREAKING NEWS🚨: According to @theinformation, Microsoft's $5B less in capex in Q3 than it had planned was in part due to delays by $IREN.\n\nWe would not be surprised by this, considering that IREN continues to come up in our conversations with neocloud customers, usually for the https://t.co/P0ESYVVebN", "entities": {"cashtags": [{"end": 136, "start": 131, "tag": "IREN"}], "mentions": [{"end": 44, "id": "1881168794", "start": 29, "username": "theinformation"}], "urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/P0ESYVVebN", "end": 302, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/SemiAnalysis_/status/2118133582979813819/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2118133580945620992", "start": 279, "url": "https://t.co/P0ESYVVebN"}]}, "url": "https://x.com/SemiAnalysis_/status/2118133582979813819"}, {"author_id": "4398626122", "created_at": "2026-11-04T23:35:14.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2118124944928432327"], "id": "2118124944928432327", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 4070, "impression_count": 2211678, "like_count": 20438, "quote_count": 1763, "reply_count": 1091, "retweet_count": 1768}, "text": "Images, upgraded—introducing ChatGPT Images 2.6.\